{
  "A list of commands that comes up from the bottom, made of the kit's menu items and large enough for a finger, with a title, a message and a cancel button apart. A context menu opens its items here on a touch screen.": "",
  "Choosing programmatically": "",
  "`choose()` opens it and resolves with the item chosen, or `null`. An item with `items` opens its submenu in place, with a way back.": "",
  "In JSX": "",
  "Bound with `x-model`; check and radio items show their marks, `cancelText` names the cancel button.": "",
  "A context menu on a touch screen": "",
  "`ContextMenu` has `presentation`: `'menu'` (the default), `'sheet'`, or `'auto'`, which opens an action sheet when a finger opened the menu (a long press). The items, `onOpening` and `onItemClick` stay the same.": "",
  "Between the items, round at the ends.": "",
  "Chooses it; on a submenu, opens it in place.": "",
  "The next item that starts with it.": "",
  "Closes it without a choice.": "",
  "To the cancel button and back.": "",
  "The sheet is a `dialog` named by its title; the items are a `menu` of `menuitem`, `menuitemcheckbox` and `menuitemradio`, as in the kit's menus.": "",
  "Opened by a key, on the first item; by a finger or the pointer, on the list. It goes back where it was when the sheet closes.": "",
  "Open in place of their menu with \"Back\" first; the arrow at the end of an item says it has one.": "",
  "Items are `control.height.lg` high (`actionsheet.item-height`), larger than the 24 pixels WCAG 2.2 asks for.": "",
  "Cancel, the way back and its default name come from `uiLocale.strings` (`cancel`, `back`, `actionSheetLabel`); `cancelText` gives one of your own.": "",
  "On the bottom sheet's layer (`.mx-bottom-sheet`), whose hooks it has.": "",
  "The menu (`.mx-menu`).": "",
  "The row of the cancel button.": "",
  "The mark of the way back.": "",
  "Units: the message, the mark of the item that goes back out of a submenu (`rtl`), the strip that holds the cancel button.": "",
  "Places: the items, large enough for a finger; the cancel button; the sheet’s content padding.": "",
  "The surface, the handle and the title, as on the bottom sheet.": "",
  "The commands: the kit's menu items, with their icons, check and radio marks, tones, `&` keys, groups and submenus (shortcuts are not shown).": "",
  "A title above the items; it names the sheet (else `label`, else \"Actions\").": "",
  "A line under the title that says what the choice is about.": "",
  "A cancel button apart, at the bottom.": "",
  "Its text; empty for `uiLocale`'s Cancel.": "",
  "As tall as its items (up to full); any of the bottom sheet's heights.": "",
  "An item was chosen, after the sheet closed and the item's own `click` ran.": "",
  "Modal, the handle, swipe down, Escape, the scrim and the back button work as on the [BottomSheet page](/bottomsheet#api).": "",
  "Opens it (with these items) and resolves with the item chosen, or `null` when it was closed without one. `host` gives it a place when it has none.": "",
  "Opens it; `byKeyboard` puts focus on the first item, else on the list as a menu the pointer opened.": "",
  "The item chosen the last time it was open.": "",
  "Its `MenuList`.": "",
  "Your items may be plain or reactive; the sheet reads them as they are. After changing them in place, call `refresh()`. The level shown follows.": "",
  "On `ContextMenu`, default `'menu'`. `'sheet'` opens its items in an action sheet; `'auto'` does when a finger opened it (a long press), or on a screen with only a coarse pointer when not opened by a key. `onOpening`, `onItemClick` and `onClosed` work the same; `actionSheet` is the sheet.": ""
}
